  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Accelerating Gender Equality in Camb</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to establish a care-centric economy by supporting the Ministry of Women&apos;s Affairs to generate evidence-based data on challenges faced by women in Unpaid Care and Domestic Work, sensitizing policymakers to integrate care-responsive policies, and raising awareness among authorities and the public. During the implementation period, Oxfam and its partners will focus on laying thefoundations for future policy change, and for behavior change among policymakers and the public.
The Theory of Change underpinning this project is that: if the relevant government actors (initially with Oxfam support) can effectively generate and share evidence and data that highlight the challenges faced by women involved in UCDW, and simultaneously raise awareness among policymakers and senior government officials, Gender Mainstreaming Action Groups (GMAGs), and other relevant authorities about the significance of evidence and of addressing UCDW in their priorities, and if the awareness and capabilities of women,CSOs, and the general public is enhanced so that they can advocate for investment in social infrastructure and challenge societal norms, then we can create an increasingly enabling environment that supports the development of a care economy, where women&#x2019;scare responsibilities are recognized, valued, and fairly shared, where evidence-based data is generated and used in supporting policy processes, raising awareness, and fostering public dialogue.</narrative>
  </description>
